    "text_analysis": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "$AEON gave back 19.2% over the past 24h, falling to $0.00001834, but the move came on just $107.0K in volume — 0.62x the 7-day average ($173.2K) — a fraction of the conviction behind Wednesday's breakout, which is why this lands as CONSOLIDATING rather than a breakdown. Whale flow (21 trades ≥$1K) was sell-heavy, 14 sells vs 7 buys: the largest prints were a $12.64K sell at $0.0000182 (18:39 UTC), a $12.21K sell at $0.0000176 (22:15 UTC), and an $8.75K buy at $0.0000175 (05:23 UTC) — that last trade lines up with a late bounce, with price up 11.2% in the final hour off session lows. Liquidity in the AEON/WETH pool thinned 14.0% to $1.18M (from $1.38M, a $192.5K pullback), tracking the price decline rather than a standalone LP exit. Buy/sell count actually flipped bullish (151/92, ratio 1.64, up from yesterday's 0.91) even as price fell — more small buyers stepping in against a handful of large sellers, consistent with distribution into weak hands rather than a broad flush.",
        "variant": "body"
      }
